:delegate-call":""},"constructor":{"details":"config Unused members: chainlinkFeed, oracleError, oracleTimeoutNo revenue hiding (refPerTok() is constant)config.erc20 should be an AerodromeStakingWrapper"},"isCollateral()":{"returns":{"_0":"If the asset is an instance of ICollateral or not"}},"lotPrice()":{"details":"Deprecated. Phased out in 3.1.0, but left on interface for backwards compatibility","returns":{"lotHigh":"{UoA/tok} The upper end of the lot price estimate","lotLow":"{UoA/tok} The lower end of the lot price estimate"}},"price()":{"details":"Should be general enough to not need to be overridden","returns":{"_high":"{UoA/tok} The upper end of the price estimate","_low":"{UoA/tok} The lower end of the price estimate"}},"refPerTok()":{"returns":{"_0":"{ref/tok} Actual quantity of whole reference units per whole collateral tokens"}},"status()":{"returns":{"_0":"The collateral's status"}},"targetPerRef()":{"returns":{"_0":"{target/ref} Quantity of whole target units per whole reference unit in the peg"}},"tokenFeeds(uint8)":{"params":{"index":"The index of the token: 0 or 1"},"returns":{"_0":"[address of chainlink feeds]"}},"tokenPrice(uint8)":{"details":"Warning: Can revert","params":{"index":"The index of the token: 0 or 1"},"returns":{"high":"{UoA/ref_index}","low":"{UoA/ref_index}"}},"tokenReserve(uint8)":{"params":{"index":"The index of the token: 0 or 1"},"returns":{"_0":"{ref_index}"}},"tryPrice()":{"returns":{"high":"{UoA/tok} The high price estimate","low":"{UoA/tok} The low price estimate","pegPrice":"{target/ref} The actual price observed in the peg"}}},"title":"AerodromeStableCollateral  This plugin contract is designed for Aerodrome stable pools  Each token in the pool can have between 1 and 2 oracles per each token. tok = AerodromeStakingWrapper(stablePool) ref = LP token /w shift tar = USD UoA = USD","version":1},"userdoc":{"errors":{"UIntOutOfBounds()":[{"notice":"The logical type `uint192 ` is a 192 bit value, representing an 18-decimal Fixed-point fractional value.  This is what's described in the Solidity documentation as \"fixed192x18\" -- a value represented by 192 bits, that makes 18 digits available to the right of the decimal point. The range of values that uint192 can represent is [0, 2^192-1 / 10^18 = 6.2e39]. Unless a function explicitly says otherwise, it will fail on overflow. To be clear, the following should hold: toFix(0) == 0 toFix(1) == 1e18"}]},"events":{"CollateralStatusChanged(uint8,uint8)":{"notice":"Emitted whenever the collateral status is changed"},"RewardsClaimed(address,uint256)":{"notice":"Emitted whenever a reward token balance is claimed"}},"kind":"user","methods":{"claimRewards()":{"notice":"Claim rewards earned by holding a balance of the ERC20 token"},"lotPrice()":{"notice":"Should not revert lotLow should be nonzero when the asset might be worth selling"},"price()":{"notice":"Should not revert low should be nonzero if the asset could be worth sellingIf the price feed is broken, _low will decay downwards and _high will decay upwards     If tryPrice() is broken for `oracleTimeout + priceTimeout + ORACLE_TIMEOUT_BUFFER` ,     _low will be 0 and _high will be FIX_MAX.     Because the price decay begins at `oracleTimeout + ORACLE_TIMEOUT_BUFFER` seconds,     the price feed can be broken for up to `2 * oracleTimeout` seconds without     affecting the price estimate.  This could happen if the Asset is refreshed just before     the maxOracleTimeout is reached, forcing a second period to pass before     the price begins to decay."},"refresh()":{"notice":"Should not revert Refresh exchange rates and update default status. Have to override to add custom default checks"},"tryPrice()":{"notice":"Can revert, used by other contract functions in order to catch errors Should not return FIX_MAX for low Should only return FIX_MAX for high if low is 0 Should NOT be manipulable by MEV"}},"version":1}},"settings":{"compilationTarget":{"contracts/plugins/assets/aerodrome/AerodromeStableCollate